# LLM provider package rules

When editing `internal/llm`:

- kprompt does **not** sell API keys. BYOK + optional local Ollama (`$0` path).
- No configured provider → stay **unconfigured**; do not silently default to OpenAI.
- Keys live in env (`KPROMPT_*` / vendor vars) or Team secrets pull — never write secrets into `~/.kprompt/config.yaml` or the repo.
- New vendors: prefer OpenAI-compatible adapter + preset row; update `docs/providers.md` and `kprompt init` help.
- Unit/CI paths use `stub` provider — tests must stay keyless.
- Team `kp_…` tokens are org policy/audit, not inference credentials.
- Preserve honest Gemini free-tier / 429 messaging when touching Gemini paths.
- Run `go test ./internal/llm/` after changes.
